WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.735 --> 00:00:15.695
"I have to get to Sunshine Coffee Shop," Roxy thought.

2
00:00:15.696 --> 00:00:19.493
"Zombies are hurting people!"

3
00:00:19.494 --> 00:00:21.750
Roxy went back to the table.

4
00:00:21.751 --> 00:00:28.946
"I just remembered. I, uh, need to help Principal Penn!"

5
00:00:28.947 --> 00:00:32.929
Roxy ran down the hall.

6
00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:43.090
She threw open the door and leaped into the sky.

7
00:00:43.091 --> 00:00:46.473
People stood outside Sunshine Coffee Shop.

8
00:00:46.474 --> 00:00:51.134
When Roxy got closer, she saw they were not normal people.

9
00:00:51.135 --> 00:00:52.966
Their eyes were blank.

10
00:00:52.967 --> 00:00:54.924
Their hair was messy.

11
00:00:54.925 --> 00:00:58.712
And they moved in a strange way.

12
00:00:58.713 --> 00:01:02.020
"Zombies!" Roxy said.

13
00:01:02.021 --> 00:01:05.089
A woman was in the doorway of Sunshine Coffee Shop.

14
00:01:05.090 --> 00:01:07.630
She was waving zombies away with a broom.

15
00:01:07.631 --> 00:01:12.533
The zombies' mouths snapped open and shut.

16
00:01:12.534 --> 00:01:16.838
"Get out of here!" the woman yelled.

17
00:01:16.839 --> 00:01:21.297
Roxy swooped down and pushed the zombies away from the door.

18
00:01:21.298 --> 00:01:24.557
Then she ran in with the woman.

19
00:01:24.558 --> 00:01:28.048
The woman locked the door behind her.

20
00:01:28.049 --> 00:01:31.723
"Whew!" The woman ran a hand across her forehead.

21
00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:36.692
"That was scary! I'm glad you're here, Rocket Girl."

22
00:01:36.693 --> 00:01:39.481
"No problem," Roxy said.

23
00:01:39.482 --> 00:01:41.851
Suddenly she spotted Detective Smith.

24
00:01:41.852 --> 00:01:45.325
He stood up near a case with only a few donuts left.

25
00:01:45.326 --> 00:01:47.677
His hair was messy.

26
00:01:47.678 --> 00:01:53.167
"Ahh!" Roxy cried. "It's another zombie!"

27
00:01:53.168 --> 00:01:54.983
Detective Smith frowned.

28
00:01:54.984 --> 00:01:57.779
"Very funny, Rocket Girl."

29
00:01:57.780 --> 00:01:59.939
He tried to pat down his hair.

30
00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:03.872
"I forgot to brush my hair this morning."

31
00:02:03.873 --> 00:02:06.024
Roxy pointed out the window.

32
00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:09.496
"What turned all those people into zombies?"

33
00:02:09.497 --> 00:02:11.772
Detective Smith scratched his head.

34
00:02:11.773 --> 00:02:16.038
His hair got messier. "I'm not sure."

35
00:02:16.039 --> 00:02:18.016
The woman pointed at the case.

36
00:02:18.017 --> 00:02:20.531
"It was those donuts."

37
00:02:20.532 --> 00:02:23.287
"How do you know?" Roxy asked.

38
00:02:23.288 --> 00:02:26.338
"A man came in earlier," she said.

39
00:02:26.339 --> 00:02:30.711
"After he ate one of the donuts, he looked strange.

40
00:02:30.712 --> 00:02:35.854
He tried to bite another customer, so I pushed him outside.

41
00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:38.834
Other people ate the donuts after that.

42
00:02:38.835 --> 00:02:42.891
The same thing happened to them."

43
00:02:42.892 --> 00:02:45.156
Detective Smith opened the case.

44
00:02:45.157 --> 00:02:47.703
He picked up a donut and studied it.

45
00:02:47.704 --> 00:02:50.960
"It looks like a regular donut to me."

46
00:02:50.961 --> 00:02:54.486
"Did this ever happen before?" Roxy asked.

47
00:02:54.487 --> 00:02:56.301
The woman shook her head.

48
00:02:56.302 --> 00:03:01.406
"Never. I just started ordering these donuts from a new bakery.

49
00:03:01.407 --> 00:03:04.287
These are the first ones I got."

50
00:03:04.288 --> 00:03:07.847
"What's the name of the bakery?" Detective Smith asked.

51
00:03:07.848 --> 00:03:10.322
"Le Sweet's," the woman said.

52
00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:14.355
"It's just outside the city, near the mountains."

53
00:03:14.356 --> 00:03:18.423
"I'll go and check it out," Roxy said.

54
00:03:18.424 --> 00:03:21.335
She ran out the door and flew off.

55
00:03:21.336 --> 00:03:25.278
Down the block she saw the door to Shop well Supermarket fly open.

56
00:03:25.279 --> 00:03:31.955
A huge pack of zombies spilled out from the door!
